Also having this on a project that uses roughly the following style function in the app directory.

Sample file location: `src/app/(auth)/auth-error/page.tsx`

We're seeing this under Next.JS versions `13.0.7` and `13.1.6`

```ts
export default function ErrorPage({
  searchParams,
}: {
  searchParams: { error?: string }
}) {
  const { error } = searchParams

  if (!error) {
    redirect('/404')
  }

  return(
    // some UI code
  )
}
```

@Ziothh Here's how we're solving this in our app in the short-term as this gets looked into—we're essentially typing the `searchParams` as any key-value pair per Next.JS beta docs. But this typing allows a string array on our searchParams key—this doesn't work for us, so we're coercing its value to either `string` or `undefined` before using it:

```ts
export function stringOrUndefined(
  value: string | string[] | undefined,
): string | undefined {
  return value === undefined ? undefined : value.toString()
}

export default function ErrorPage({
  searchParams,
}: {
  searchParams: [key: string]: string | string[] | undefined
}) {
  const error = stringOrUndefined(searchParams.error)

  if (!error) {
    redirect('/404')
  }

  return(
    // some UI code
  )
}
```

I'm running next.js 13.1.6. I had this same error. Fixed with:

```ts
import type { PageComponent } from '../../../../.next/types/app/page';

const InscriptionDetailPage: PageComponent = async ({
  params: { name },
}: {
  params: { name: string };
}) => {
```

next.js should probably export `PageComponent` for us.

